Why This Is Asked\n\nThis question probes understanding of practical sorting trade-offs beyond textbook asymptotics, including cache locality, in-place constraints, and robust pivot strategies. It invites discussion of 3-way partitioning to handle duplicates, median-of-three to curb worst-case behavior, and a small insertion sort for tiny partitions.\n\n## Key Concepts\n- 3-way partitioning in quicksort\n- median-of-three pivot selection\n- insertion sort threshold tuning\n- in-place algorithms and cache efficiency\n- iterative vs recursive implementations\n\n## Code Example\n```javascript
function sortInPlace(arr){
  const TH = 16;
  const swap=(a,i,j)=>{const t=a[i]; a[i]=a[j]; a[j]=t;};
  const medianOfThree=(a,i,j,k)=>{let x=[a[i],i],[a[j],j],[a[k],k].sort((p,q)=>p[0]-q[0]); return a[x[1]];};
  // iterative 3-way quicksort skeleton
  const stack=[[0,arr.length-1]];
  while(stack.length){
    const [lo,hi]=stack.pop();
    if(hi-lo+1<=TH){ // insertion sort for small partitions
      for(let i=lo+1;i<=hi;i++){
        let t=arr[i], j=i-1;
        while(j>=lo && arr[j]>t){ arr[j+1]=arr[j]; j-- }
        arr[j+1]=t;
      }
      continue;
    }
    // median-of-three pivot
    const mid=(lo+hi)>>1;
    const pivot= medianOfThree(arr, lo, mid, hi);
    // 3-way partition
    let lt=lo, i=lo, gt=hi;
    while(i<=gt){
      if(arr[i]<pivot) swap(arr, lt++, i++);
      else if(arr[i]>pivot) swap(arr, i, gt--);
      else i++;
    }
    stack.push([lo, lt-1]);
    stack.push([gt+1, hi]);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates understanding of the Trie (prefix tree) data structure, covering insert, delete, and prefix-query operations with proper edge case handling.

## Key Concepts

- **Trie node structure**: Each node stores 26 child pointers, an end-of-word flag, and a pass-through counter for efficient prefix queries
- **Safe deletion**: Decrement counts along the path and only unmark end-of-word when the word actually exists
- **Prefix query**: Return the count at the prefix's last node in O(length of prefix) time
- **Duplicate handling**: Adding the same word twice increments the counter twice; deleting decrements twice, effectively removing one occurrence

## Code Example

```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.children = new Array(26).fill(null);
    this.isEndOfWord = false;
    this.count = 0;
  }
}

class Trie {
  constructor() {
    this.root = new TrieNode();
  }

  add(word) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of word) {
      const index = char.charCodeAt(0) - 97;
      if (!node.children[index]) {
        node.children[index] = new TrieNode();
      }
      node = node.children[index];
      node.count++;
    }
    node.isEndOfWord = true;
  }

  delete(word) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of word) {
      const index = char.charCodeAt(0) - 97;
      if (!node.children[index]) return;
      node = node.children[index];
      node.count--;
    }
    node.isEndOfWord = false;
  }

  countPrefix(prefix) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of prefix) {
      const index = char.charCodeAt(0) - 97;
      if (!node.children[index]) return 0;
      node = node.children[index];
    }
    return node.count;
  }
}
```

